text
> Install guide
>
> Run make check first: it is fast and strict, not ~~slow~~ (a
> single newline is a space here), and both. See usage or the
> site, or https://example.org. A line ending in two spaces
> breaks.
>
> Lists
>
> • first item that is long enough to wrap onto a second line
>   when drawn
> • second
>   1. nested one
>   2. nested two
> • third
>
> 3. three
> 4. four
>
> ▎ Measure twice, cut once.
>
> ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
>
>  func main() {
>
>      println("hi")
>  }
>
>  indented code
>
> Raw <b>HTML</b> stays text, and so does:
>
> <div onclick="x()">a block</div>
>
> [the diagram] and a script link.
>
> Usage
>
> The end.
